     -$11,371 card balance permanently flagged low).
     MASTER get_balance_projection: available=true, crossing="2026-09-04",
     minimum=-14921.22, suggested_top_up=15500 (nonsense top-up on a card).
     FIX get_accounts: low_balance=false, threshold=0 (matches contract).
     FIX get_balance_projection: TOOL-ERROR "account \"usaa-credit-card\" has
     kind \"credit\"; the funding projection and low-balance threshold apply
     only to checking and savings accounts" (matches contract).
   - usaa-checking / usaa-health-checking (kind "checking"): byte-identical
     across both trees (low_balance=false, threshold=500, balance/minimum
     unchanged) — the fix is protective-only for real checking data, no
     regression.
   CONCLUSION: real-data probe proves the fix is a genuine, verified bugfix
   on the live ledger, not a no-op.

2. SURFACE ENUMERATION: grepped LowBalance/low_balance/threshold across all
   .go/.md/.html/.js. Enumerated consumers: dashboard accounts_card.go (2
   sites: state switch + projection eligibility, both gated), MCP
   accounts.go get_accounts + get_balance_projection (both gated),
   internal/services/accounts/balance.go (no threshold logic — clean),
   internal/handlers/accounts/handlers.go (/accounts settings page — only
   edits the LowBalanceThreshold VALUE, never computes/renders a low_balance
   comparison, so it is not a "surface reporting a flag" and needs no gate).
   Templates accounts.html and accounts_card.html only render values the
   gated Go code already computed — no independent comparison in template
   logic. No unlisted comparison surface found. Full package test suite
   (accounts, dashboard, mcpsvc/ledger) green in the fix tree.

3. EDGE ATTACKS:
   - Unknown/empty kind: LowBalanceApplies("") and LowBalanceApplies(any
     non-enum string) both return false (fails safe — non-applicable, never
     over-flagged). handlers.go already defaults an omitted/unknown kind to
     "other" at write time, so this is consistent and documented behavior,
     confirmed by TestLowBalanceApplies pinning the closed enum
     (checking=true, savings=true, brokerage/credit/other=false).
   - Savings: same OR-condition as checking in LowBalanceApplies, no
     separate code path exists that could special-case it — no
     over-suppression risk found.
   - threshold=0 on checking: thresholdFor's `> 0` check (unchanged by this
     diff, present on master too) means 0 still means "use default 500",
     not "no threshold" — pre-existing ambiguity, NOT introduced by LB1,
     out of scope for this task.
   - available=false interaction: dashboard routes to accountStateNoAnchor
     BEFORE the LowBalanceApplies switch case runs (confirmed by reading
     the code — the `if !balance.Available {...} else { switch {...} }`
     structure), and MCP get_accounts only sets LowBalance when
     `bal.Available` (unchanged logic, now additionally kind-gated). The
     gate does not re-enable flagging for unavailable balances on either
     surface.

4. STALE-DOC HUNT (ND3 class) — FAIL basis:
   internal/models/account.go:9-12 (UNTOUCHED by this diff — confirmed via
   `git diff --cached --name-only`, the file is not listed) states:
     "One behavioral consequence, and only one: AccountKindCredit forces
     the credit-card sign convention for every CSV file that belongs to
     the account... Every other kind leaves that heuristic exactly as it
     is."
   GLOSSARY.md:87 makes the same claim ("One behavioral consequence: `Kind:
   credit` **forces** the credit-card sign convention... Other kinds leave
   the heuristic alone.").
   Both are now FALSE: this diff gives AccountKind a SECOND behavioral
   consequence — LowBalanceApplies(kind) now gates the low-balance flag and
   funding projection on every enumerated surface, per the new function's
   own doc comment in projection.go ("Every surface that reports a
   low-balance flag or a funding projection... must gate on this"). The
   account.go comment's explicit "and only one" claim, sitting directly on
   the AccountKind type this task's central function switches on, is
   falsified by the worker's own change and was not updated. (Contrast:
   the adjacent Account.LowBalanceThreshold field comment at account.go:62
   already said "only meaningful for the checking and savings kinds" before
   this diff — that one predicted the fix and is fine; the AccountKind
   type-level "and only one" comment is the one this diff breaks.)
   This sits inside the same package/type the task's contract is built on
   (accounts.LowBalanceApplies(kind), internal/models.AccountKind) — not an
   unrelated pre-existing doc drift — and is a direct, mechanical
   consequence of leaving this task incomplete, analogous to the CB3-b
   precedent (SPEC.md rulings) where an adjacent tool-docstring surface
