VERDICT: FAIL — internal/models/account.go's AccountKind doc comment (and
GLOSSARY.md's mirror of it) make an explicit "and only one" /
"one behavioral consequence" claim about AccountKind that this diff's own
new LowBalanceApplies function falsifies. This is the ND3 stale-doc class
the task was explicitly dispatched to hunt, sits inside the same type the
task's contract is built on, and was not touched by the diff. Real-data
probe (section 1) otherwise confirms the functional fix is correct and a
genuine bugfix (live low_balance=true/suggested_top_up=15500 on
usaa-credit-card on master, corrected on the fix branch) — this FAIL is
about the doc-comment omission, not the runtime behavior.
